# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Course requirement: no media in GitHub.
# Every .mp4 and .mp3 lives in course media storage and is linked from the
# repository README. MEDIA.md is the manifest: every excluded file with its
# SHA-256, so an uploaded copy can be verified against this repo.
#
# Nothing that makes the film auditable is excluded: the beat sheet, the
# coverage contract, every input log, the capture driver, the export receipt
# and all reports stay in git.
#
# NOTE: coverage.json records the SHA-256 of each capture, so on a fresh clone
# `./art godot-waikthrough --check` fails with "Missing/empty evidence" until
# capture/*.mp4 is restored from course media storage. The evidence chain
# survives the media leaving git; it just cannot be re-checked without it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.mp3

# The root .gitignore excludes exports/ wholesale. Re-include just the
# hash-bound export receipt — git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the path has to be opened up level by level.
!exports/
exports/*
!exports/landscape/
exports/landscape/*
!exports/landscape/*.verified.json

# Regenerable build intermediates — rebuild with BUILD-PROMPT.md.
clips/
qc-sheet.png
_qc/frames/
